{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "One of the eight basic Allomantic metals. An Allomancer burning it sees blue lines pointing to nearby metal and can Pull that metal toward themselves.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "final-empire", "chapter": "7" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "A metal used by all three metal-based arts. Allomancers burn it to Pull on metal, Feruchemists store weight in it, and Hemalurgic spikes of iron steal physical strength.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "final-empire", "chapter": "7" },
            { "book": "well-of-ascension", "chapter": "53" },
            { "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "42" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Alone, iron is mostly defensive, for instance Pulling enemy projectiles into a wooden shield, and it needs a heavy, anchored piece of metal to fly toward. Used together with steel it is far more powerful.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "final-empire", "chapter": "34" },
            { "book": "well-of-ascension", "chapter": "2" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Feruchemist can store weight in iron and tap it to grow heavier, for example to brace against a force or strike harder.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "well-of-ascension", "chapter": "58" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Koloss are made by driving iron spikes into a living human, giving great strength but ruining the mind. Kandra call a pair of iron spikes the Blessing of Potency, which grants strength and endurance.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "40" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "The force of a Pull grows with the Allomancer's own weight, and metal partly inside a person's body normally cannot be Pulled, though a strong enough Lurcher can overcome both limits.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "final-empire", "chapter": "7" },
            { "book": "alloy-of-law", "chapter": "prologue" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Roshar, a fabrial with an iron cage attracts the element tied to its trapped spren, such as smoke.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "11" }]
    }
  ],
